  {
    "type": "post",
    "title": "Embention",
    "company": "Embention",
    "location": "",
    "text": "Six times more RF spectrum coverage. Four times more processing and AI compute. Thirty-one times more storage. Those are some of the gains behind DroneShield ’s new RfRecon platform, which combines RF sensing, direction finding, and RfAI-3 intelligence in a portable system designed to improve tactical spectrum awareness and support faster decision-making. Elsewhere, Greensea IQ has introduced Bayonet Sweep, an autonomous underwater robot designed to inspect ship hulls and harbor infrastructure for potential threats without requiring manual diver sweeps. Embention USA and SkyRunner, LLC are integrating Veronte Autopilot with the MK 3.2 dual-mode air-ground vehicle to add autonomous and remote-piloted capabilities, while Iridium examines how satellite connectivity can support C2, tracking, and data communications for long-range BVLOS drone operations. At the computing layer, Wolf Advanced Technology explores the growing role of compact, rugged edge computing for AI, video, networking, and sensor processing in European defense applications. Looking further ahead, UTES2026 will bring together industry, academia, and research at Chalmers University of Technology to explore autonomous technologies spanning uncrewed aviation, advanced air mobility, and future space missions. Catch up on the full stories in this week’s Unmanned Systems Technology newsletter ⬇️",
