    "title": "prg.ai",
    "company": "prg.ai",
    "location": "",
    "text": "🏆 On its debut at the International Olympiad in Artificial Intelligence (IOAI) , the Czech National AI Team brought home two medals. In Astana, Kazakhstan, Patrik Řezníček took bronze, and Jan Herza went one better with silver. The Czechs held their own among 440 competitors from 95 countries and regions. Over two six-hour rounds and six tasks, they had to quickly read the input data and metrics and turn their ideas into a working solution. The Czech National AI Team emerged from the first edition of the Česká AI Olympiáda organised by nvias.org . We are glad that prg.ai , as a partner of the event, could support the Prague regional round – helping with its organisation, funding, and securing mentors and the expert jury. The success of Czech students on the international stage means a great deal to us, and we will be following the team's next steps closely.",
